From 338829223f339c7d111677b21bf2ff9dc8b3b3ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:59:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 101/109] drm/msm/dp: don't write LINK_BW_SET before
 LINK_RATE_SET

dp_panel only selects the eDP 1.4 rate table when LINK_BW_SET already
reads 0, so the write of 0 before LINK_RATE_SET is not needed. i915
stopped writing it in commit e6861d8264cd ("drm/i915/edp: don't write
to DP_LINK_BW_SET when using rate select") after a panel ignored
LINK_RATE_SET following that write. Drop it, as in the upstream form of
this fix.

On the ASUS Zenbook A16 the panel trains through LINK_RATE_SET without
the write once the compositor re-reads the link caps.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 13 -------------
 1 file changed, 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index 4be864b8eca5..be985dea31e9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -234,19 +234,6 @@ static int msm_dp_aux_link_configure(struct drm_dp_aux *aux,
 		return err < 0 ? err : -EIO;
 
 	if (link->use_rate_set) {
-		/*
-		 * Per eDP 1.4b, LINK_RATE_SET is only consulted while
-		 * LINK_BW_SET reads 00h, so the legacy selector has to be
-		 * cleared before the rate-set one is written. Drivers that
-		 * never touch LINK_BW_SET get this for free; we cannot assume
-		 * it, because firmware may have trained the panel and left its
-		 * own selection behind (on the ASUS Zenbook A16 the UEFI
-		 * leaves DP_LINK_BW_5_4 there).
-		 */
-		err = drm_dp_dpcd_writeb(aux, DP_LINK_BW_SET, 0);
-		if (err != 1)
-			return err < 0 ? err : -EIO;
-
 		DRM_DEBUG_DP("using LINK_RATE_SET: 0x%02x", link->rate_set);
 		err = drm_dp_dpcd_writeb(aux, DP_LINK_RATE_SET, link->rate_set);
 	} else {
